# ============================================================
# File:        deploy.yml.disabled
# Path:        .github/workflows/deploy.yml.disabled
# Project:     RaceArena
# Created:     2026-04-19
# Description: INTENT ONLY — this workflow has NEVER RUN, not once, and cannot run as written.
#
# THIS FILE IS A RECORD, NOT A PIPELINE. It is kept deliberately: deleting it would delete the
# record of a decision, and this project's rule is that doing so is how a project forgets why.
#
# ── THE `.disabled` SUFFIX IS THE MECHANISM, AND IT IS WHY THIS FILE WAS RENAMED ────────────────
#
# The header below has said "never run, cannot run" since 2026-08-04 — and GitHub still listed this
# workflow as **active** (`gh workflow list` reported: `Deploy  active  272257209`). A prose
# disclaimer inside a registered workflow is invisible to the platform and to anyone reading the
# Actions tab, and CHECK-AUDIT-1 flagged exactly that: a configuration that looks live while being
# documented as dormant.
#
# GitHub registers only `*.yml` / `*.yaml` under `.github/workflows/`. Ending the name `.disabled`
# de-registers it entirely — it leaves the Actions list — while the file stays exactly where a
# reader looking for the deployment thinking would go, with its content untouched.
#
# WHY NOT the alternatives: disabling it through the API is repo state, invisible in the tree, and
# reverts on a whim; moving it under docs/ separates it from the other workflows a reader compares
# it against; changing the trigger to `workflow_dispatch` would leave it registered AND make it
# easier to fire, which is the opposite of the intent.
#
# TO REVIVE IT: rename back to `deploy.yml` AND clear all four blockers below. The rename alone
# would register a workflow that still cannot work.
#
# Measured at origin on 2026-08-04 (CI-AUDIT-GREEN-1 §10): the Deploy workflow is registered and
# ACTIVE but has 0 runs in its entire history; the last 100 Actions runs are 100% CI; and the repo
# has 0 deployments, 0 environments, 0 webhooks, 0 deploy keys and no Pages site.
#
# FOUR things would have to change before it could work:
#   1. the trigger is `branches: [main]`; the only branch at origin is `master`
#   2. `scripts/deploy.sh` does not exist in this repository
#   3. all three secrets it consumes are absent — DEPLOY_HOST, DEPLOY_USER, DEPLOY_KEY
#   4. RA_PUBLIC_ORIGIN exists only as the placeholder racearena.example.com
#
# Deployment today is MANUAL and the server runs only on the owner's machine — nothing is online.
# See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md for the by-hand production start and docs/BACKLOG.md, "Before the VPS
# migration", for what must be settled first. Do not "fix" this file into life by accident: making
# it run would start publishing to production.
# ============================================================

name: Deploy

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - name: Deploy via SSH
        uses: appleboy/ssh-action@v1
        with:
          host: ${{ secrets.DEPLOY_HOST }}
          username: ${{ secrets.DEPLOY_USER }}
          key: ${{ secrets.DEPLOY_KEY }}
          script: |
            cd /srv/racearena
            git pull origin main
            bash scripts/deploy.sh
